Author: whycz <whyczz@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 17 00:52:20 2026 -0500

    test(mvp.5): Pi process-tree proof — bubble once, tree dead, fresh revival
    
    For humans: the five Pi acceptance rows now have a real
    root -> node-worker -> edge-worker process-tree drive:
    one facts-only blocked bubble, process-table death,
    parent_run_id grandchild disposition, fresh-tree revival.
    
    For LLMs: test/pi-tree.test.mjs spawns real OS worker
    processes claiming real bp3 links against a fixture repo,
    asserts bubble/run-chain/inbox facts, kill(pid,0) death,
    watch orphaned disposition, and new-root revival from
    rollup+inbox. Wired into make check and node --check lint.

